      <Comment source="pmngroup">Several lines of evidence suggest that this enzyme is involved in the first of two demethylation steps that occur during plant sterol biosynthesis |CITS: [14653780]|. It should be capable of performing the reaction: a 4,4-dimethyl-9&amp;beta;,19-cyclopropylsterol + 3NADPH + 3H+ + 3O2 -&gt; a 4&amp;alpha;-carboxy, 4&amp;beta;-methyl-9&amp;beta;,19-cyclopropylsterol) + 3NADP+ + 3H2O. Enzymes of this class carry out three successive monooxygenation steps on the methyl group causing it to undergo the following series of changes: CH3-&gt;CH2OH-&gt;CHO-&gt;COOH. The final product of these reactions can then be acted on by a 3&amp;beta;-hydroxysteroid-dehydrogenase/C4-decarboxylase and a 3-keto-reductase to produce the final monomethylated product |CITS: [14653780]|. But, to date, no direct assays of this enzyme&apos;s activities have been performed.</Comment>
